  "source": "[\\integer.pair.add]\nDefines: add(a_, b_) is \\binary.operation:on{\\integer.pair.carrier}\nexpresses:\n. forAll: a1, b1, a2, b2 is \\natural\n  then: add(\\integer.pair.class:of{a1, b1}, \\integer.pair.class:of{a2, b2}) = \\integer.pair.class:of{a1 \\.natural.+./ a2, b1 \\.natural.+./ b2}\nDocumented:\n. called: \"integer-pair addition\"\n. written: \"a_? +_{\\mathbb{Z}} b_?\"\n. description: \"Addition induced on equivalence classes by\n                $[(a,b)] + [(c,d)] = [(a+c,b+d)]$.\"\nId: \"720771d7-3535-4c2a-864a-868fb794656c\"",
